// Version holds for releases that broke a workload after Renovate merged them.
//
// Written by Hermes (cluster-alert-triage) when it reverts a Renovate commit:
// one entry per broken release, so Renovate stops re-proposing exactly that
// version but still takes the next one. Each entry lands in the same
// "fix(alert): revert ..." commit as the revert it belongs to.
// Remove an entry once upstream ships a fixed release or the cause is known.
//
// Entry shape (enabled:false + matchNewValue rather than allowedVersions: this
// preset loads before .renovaterc.json5's own rules, whose allowedVersions would
// override a hold here, and nothing there sets enabled:true):
//   {
//     description: ["<date> <workload>: <symptom>. Reverted <commit sha>."],
//     matchDatasources: ["docker"],
//     matchPackageNames: ["<package as Renovate names it>"],
//     matchNewValue: "<exact broken tag/version as written in the reverted diff>",
//     enabled: false,
//   },
{
  packageRules: [],
}
